                    {
                        "sense_id": "f190700c-08f8-3eec-8e7b-767edc9813d6",
                        "entry_id": "aa5d1f78-e88b-3454-ad22-df7bcfea4aae",
                        "glosses": [
                            "not derived, not related."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d65a0cb0-ff46-490d-a003-bf1081afbb91",
                                "sense_id": "f190700c-08f8-3eec-8e7b-767edc9813d6",
                                "text": "If their rights are inherent and underived, they may, by their own suffrages, encircle, with a diadem, the brows of Mr. Cushing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "33853fb7-a557-4da0-b21b-f464b8022e61",
                                "sense_id": "f190700c-08f8-3eec-8e7b-767edc9813d6",
                                "text": "\"Firstly,--if underived virtue be peculiar to the Deity, can it be the duty of a creature to have it?\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac456889-aebd-4017-a697-370cc07f277b",
                                "sense_id": "f190700c-08f8-3eec-8e7b-767edc9813d6",
                                "text": "Thus it is that though contact of the senses with the objects may later on be imagined to be the conditioning factor, yet the rise of knowledge as well as our notion of its validity strikes us as original, underived, immediate, and first-hand."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c8085161-1c88-4a8e-af2d-59d4116f30b0",
                                "sense_id": "f190700c-08f8-3eec-8e7b-767edc9813d6",
                                "text": "He held that everything in existence is composed of four underived and indestructible substances--fire, water, earth, and air--and that atmosphere is a corporeal substance, not a mere void."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
